The hexagon-dsp-binaries* packages ship binaries whose versions must
match the firmware version shipped by this (firmware-qcom-dsp) package.
For this reason, this (firmware-qcom-dsp) package has taken over the
task of shipping the relevant firmwares from the previous
firmware-qcom-soc package. firmware-qcom-soc is produced by
src:firmware-nonfree, which made the necessary version matching tricky.

By moving the firmware over to firmware-qcom-dsp, this
(firmware-qcom-dsp) package can be produced by src:hexagon-dsp-binaries
instead.

This way all the files whose versions must match are produced by the
same packaging source tree, making the necessary version matching
straightforward.

This change took place in Debian unstable since
src:firmware-nonfree/firmware-qcom-soc 20251125-1.

However, for this backport to trixie, matching this change has yet to be
considered in trixie.

For this reason, the following hack is implemented.

firmware-qcom-dsp declares an unversioned Replaces on firmware-qcom-soc.
Every file shipped by firmware-qcom-dsp that is also present in
firmware-qcom-soc is taken over.

This results in the required behaviour, except in the case that
this (firmware-qcom-dsp) package is removed. In this case, it is
necessary to reinstall firmware-qcom-soc to restore the original files.

To do this, you can run:

    apt install --reinstall firmware-qcom-soc
